files.content/tools.md:
@group Interactive tools
@chapter tools.grapher
@title Graph plotter
@level tool
@summary Type any function of \(x\) and see its graph. Add sliders for \(a\), \(b\), \(c\) and \(d\) to explore transformations.

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="graph" data-edit="1" data-fns="a*sin(b*(x - c)) + d; x^2/4 - 2" data-x="-8,8" data-y="-6,6" data-params="a=2,-5,5,0.1; b=1,0.1,4,0.1; c=0,-4,4,0.1; d=0,-4,4,0.1"></div>
:::

@chapter tools.periodic
@title Periodic table
@level tool
@summary All 118 elements with relative atomic masses, groups, periods and electron configurations. Select an element to see its details.

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="periodic"></div>
:::

@chapter tools.calc
@title Calculators
@level tool
@summary Small tools for the calculations you will do again and again: relative formula mass, UCAS points, break-even, investment appraisal and unit conversions.

## Relative formula mass

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="molar"></div>
:::

## UCAS tariff points

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="ucas"></div>
:::

## Break-even

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="breakeven"></div>
:::

## Investment appraisal

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="npv"></div>
:::

## Units and prefixes

:::html
<div class="widget" data-w="units"></div>
:::

@chapter tools.glossary
@title Glossary
@level tool
@summary Every key term defined in the guide, in one searchable list. Each entry links back to the chapter that explains it.

:::html
<div id="glossaryApp"></div>
:::

files.content/practice.md:
@group Practice
@chapter practice.quiz
@title Practice quizzes
@level tool
@summary Mixed multiple-choice questions drawn from every chapter. Pick a subject and a length, answer, and get a list of chapters to revise.

:::html
<div id="practiceApp"></div>
:::

:::tip How to use quizzes well
Quizzes are retrieval practice: the act of pulling an answer out of memory is what makes it stick. Do a short quiz at the start of each study session on topics from last week, not just today's topic. When you get one wrong, open the chapter it came from and redo the worked examples before trying again.
:::

